 ## Workflow
 
-1. Inspect the existing game, design docs, build and analytics; name genre, target devices, session length and the core loop.
-2. Brainstorm, then converge: cross-examine the loop for dead ends, exploits, economy sinks and missing failure/recovery before screen work. Diagram loops and state machines as text.
-3. Plan the first-time experience: one mechanic at a time, action over text, skip/replay, measurable steps. Treat benchmarks as hypotheses.
-4. Specify screens: thumb-reach actions, 48dp or larger targets, HUD clear of fingers and cutouts, pause and interruption states.
-5. Layer feedback by event importance, return to rest, and keep it off input latency. Read [feel and touch UI](references/feel-and-touch.md) before specifying motion, haptics, HUD or controls.
-6. Offer settings for reduced shake and flashing, text size, colour-independent cues, remapping and mute. Keep copy honest, localisable.
-7. Verify on a real or emulated device at small and large widths in both orientations. Hand off screen contract, assets and evidence.
