 ## Workflow
 
-1. Inspect the engine, build files, manifest, input, save and ad/billing code; keep the existing engine unless evidence shows a blocker.
-2. For a new game, compare engines on the owner's needs (team skills, 2D or 3D, size, build time, plugins, licence) and test a small prototype on a low-end device before committing.
-3. Handle input and lifecycle: pointer-indexed multi-touch, pause on interruption, save on pause, audio focus, back and gesture navigation, cutouts and insets.
-4. Support resizing and large screens: apps targeting API 36 have orientation and aspect locks ignored at 600dp or wider; test portrait, landscape, split and foldable windows.
-5. Measure before tuning: frame time, memory, battery, thermal and install size on target hardware. Read [engine and release notes](references/engines-and-release.md) for engine, delivery or Play features.
-6. Keep secrets, ads, billing and analytics behind consent and policy review; add no engine, plugin or MCP bridge without approval.
-7. Verify with a build, tests and a run on a device or emulator; state which. Release and upload need explicit approval for the exact action.
+1. Inspect engine, build, manifest, input, saves and services; preserve project conventions.
+2. For new games compare team skills, 2D/3D, size, tooling and license; measure a small prototype on target hardware. Inspect version-matched official demos when useful.
+3. Native Android pointer IDs persist while indices change; resolve each event's index from its ID. Respect engine touch APIs. Clear held actions on cancel/pause/menu; prevent UI taps reaching gameplay. Handle saves, audio focus, back and insets.
+4. Verify SDK, category and actual windows against current Android guidance: API 36 overrides at sw600dp have a game-category exception. Test applicable rotation, resize, split and foldable states; recheck future SDK rules.
+5. Measure before tuning: frame time, memory, thermal, battery and size on target hardware. Read [engine and release notes](references/engines-and-release.md) for platform/tooling sources.
+6. Services, assets and editor bridges follow consent, policy and owner authorization. Install no engine/plugin/MCP bridge without approval.
